//! Error: `@value struct Foo { ... }` is rejected at parse time
//! Tags: parser, value, structs

//=== TEST CASE: value_annotation_on_struct_Generic ===
// `@value struct` was an alias for the canonical `value Foo { ... }`
// keyword form. The two spellings drifted: the annotation form set
// `is_value` without `is_c_repr`, so codegen scalarized callers but
// never emitted the `Foo_ct(...)` ctor. Mirrors the earlier retirement
// of `struct(C)` syntax — only one canonical declaration form.
@value
struct Vr {
    x: float,
    y: float,
}

fn main() {}
